WEBVTT

NOTE Live recording on a real Shopify store. Matches the captions burned into the video; times are set in design/video/build.sh.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A real Shopify store, running Anchorly
Larkfield Outfitters is a demo brand with 17 products. Every answer here is the live assistant.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:31.400
Finds products by how they look
The tote has no description at all. The match comes from its photo, described once at sync.

3
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:49.700
Prices and stock, read at the moment of asking
“It” is resolved from the conversation, then checked against the catalogue.

4
00:00:49.700 --> 00:01:27.900
The shopper adds to cart — the AI never does
Cards come from the catalogue. One tap adds through Shopify’s own cart, then View cart or Checkout.

5
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:54.700
Matches what shoppers mean
“Hiking in the rain” finds the waterproof boot first. Products with sizes offer Choose size.

6
00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:09.900
Size by size, never a guess
US 11 is sold out — and it says so.

7
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:26.300
Says when the store doesn’t sell it
No tents in the catalogue, so no tents are invented.

8
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:50.000
If you haven’t written it, it won’t make it up
No refund policy is published, so it offers to take the shopper’s email for the store.
